---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import { getKoUrl, getEnUrl } from '../../i18n';

const siteBase = Astro.site?.toString() || 'https://errorledger.com';
const rawPath = Astro.url.pathname.replace(/\/$/, '');
const koUrl = getKoUrl(siteBase, rawPath);
const enUrl = getEnUrl(siteBase, rawPath);
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" class="dark">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="Privacy Policy | ErrorLedger"
      description="ErrorLedger's privacy policy. We collect no personal data, require no login, and store only local browser preferences (localStorage). 100% client-side."
      lang="en"
      hreflangKo={koUrl}
      hreflangEn={enUrl}
    />
  </head>
  <body class="static-page-body">
    <Header />

    <main class="static-page-main">
      <div class="content-container">
        <span class="pill-label">Legal & Privacy</span>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="updated-date"><em>Last updated: September 2026</em></p>

        <p>
          <strong>ErrorLedger</strong> takes your privacy seriously. This policy explains what information is handled when you use our service and how it is protected.
        </p>

        <hr class="divider" />

        <h2>1. Core Principle: Local-First & Zero-Log Architecture</h2>
        <p>
          ErrorLedger runs entirely on client-side web technologies. We do not require any account registration or login, and we never collect or store your personal identity, credentials, or profile data on remote server databases.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Browser Local Storage (localStorage) Usage</h2>
        <p>
          Solely to preserve your settings and provide work continuity across sessions, the following preference data is saved locally on your device's <strong>localStorage</strong>:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Broadcast Games:</strong> Participant names, custom wheel items, penalty presets, sound mute states (<code>aether_sound_muted</code>), and theme modes</li>
          <li><strong>Stream Schedule Studio:</strong> Active timetable drafts, platform selections, time slot text, and local JSON template export/import configurations</li>
          <li><strong>Scientific MBTI:</strong> Temporary quiz state and selected question responses</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This data never leaves your device. You can erase it at any time by clearing your browser cache and site data.</p>

        <h2>3. Chzzk Downloader Local Processing & Cookie Security</h2>
        <p>
          The <strong>Chzzk Downloader</strong> distributed through ErrorLedger is a standalone desktop utility that runs on your local machine (hosted on <code>localhost:5000</code>).
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Zero Remote Transmission:</strong> Target video URLs, download progress, and saved MP4 video files are never routed to or stored on ErrorLedger servers. Downloads connect directly from official Naver CDN servers straight to your computer.</li>
          <li><strong>Adult Cookie Protection:</strong> If you input Naver login cookies (<code>NID_AUT</code>, <code>NID_SES</code>) to download 19+ age-restricted streams, these credentials remain strictly stored in your local computer memory and are only used for direct session validation with Naver servers. They are never transmitted or logged anywhere externally.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Bzzk Security Radar Data Policy</h2>
        <p>
          Bzzk Radar aggregates publicly broadcasted moderation actions across live Naver Chzzk channels to help streamers preemptively defend against malicious raids.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>No private chats, direct messages, or personal chatter data are ever recorded or monitored.</li>
          <li>All account identifiers and nicknames displayed on radar boards are <strong>100% automatically pseudonymized and masked</strong> to protect user privacy.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Scientific MBTI & Psychological Test Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Scoring for the 60-item MBTI test and calculations of the 8 Jungian cognitive function stacks (Ni, Ne, Si, Se, Ti, Te, Fi, Fe) occur <strong>100% client-side inside your browser's JavaScript runtime</strong>. Individual responses and test results are never stored or transmitted to remote databases.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Advertisements & Third-Party Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          To maintain 100% free access for all creators, ErrorLedger may serve non-intrusive advertisements via Google AdSense in compliance with <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Standard cookies may be used for statistical traffic analysis and ad delivery. You can opt out of personalized ads at any time via <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ad Settings</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Streamer Mode:</strong> Appending <code>?stream=true</code> or <code>?obs=true</code> to any URL completely disables ad scripts — zero ad cookies are set during live broadcasts.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>7. Technical Server Logs</h2>
        <p>
          Standard web server logs (IP address, browser type, timestamp, referral URLs) may be temporarily captured for network security, rate limiting, and DDoS mitigation purposes only.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions regarding this Privacy Policy or your data rights, please contact us at <a href="mailto:contact@errorledger.com">contact@errorledger.com</a> or via our <a href="/en/contact">Contact Page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .static-page-body {
    background: #090d16;
    color: #e2e8f0;
    min-height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .static-page-main {
    flex: 1;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 1.5rem 6rem;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .content-container {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .pill-label {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: #a855f7;
    background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.12);
    border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.25);
    padding: 0.25rem 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    color: #f8fafc;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .updated-date {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: #64748b;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .divider {
    border: none;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.07);
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: #f1f5f9;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0.75rem;
  }

  p, li {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: #94a3b8;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
  }

  li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }

  a { color: #38bdf8; text-decoration: none; }
  a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  code {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    padding: 0.1rem 0.3rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: #38bdf8;
  }
</style>
